WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.717
This is BotFolio.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.657
You type one sentence,
and Claude raises an AI trader.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.820
It trades play money on QIE mainnet,
and you coach it.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.880
Built for newcomers on phones.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.300
Every live claim here comes
with a receipt you can check.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:22.220
Sign-up is one sentence and a passkey,
so there's no seed phrase to lose.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:30.830
Claude writes each new bot: a name,
a personality, two limits you can change.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.810
Launch takes one signature.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:36.547
Here's Dad's Gold Guard's launch on QIE.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.190
Our relayer sent it and paid the gas.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.440
But the signer is the owner's own wallet,
and it still holds zero QIE.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:51.470
Four times a day,
every bot decides on its own.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:54.727
The AI gets the latest
prices and holdings,

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.710
and answers in strict JSON, with a reason.

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.507
Then a deterministic risk gate,
plain tested code,

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.270
clips anything over the limits
and skips stale coins.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.570
And it explains itself.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.670
Even a hold comes with a reason,
in character.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.900
Every trade card links
to its receipt on QIE.

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:23.850
This batch came from our runner:
seven trades, three bots, one transaction.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:30.157
Look inside the orders:
bot, coin, buy or sell, and size.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.780
There's no price in them.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:37.080
The contract reads the price from QIE's
oracle itself, and logs the round.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:41.000
Ask the oracle for round fifteen oh fifty:
same number.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.020
Every trade is settled against
QIE's official mainnet oracle.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.960
Stale price?
That coin holds; the batch goes on.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:56.120
Season zero opened on chain
on November twenty seventh, India time.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.220
Its close commits a root
of every decision.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:02.627
Anyone can run this replay command:

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:06.410
it re-checks every gate result
and every oracle round.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.537
The AI's answers aren't reproducible,
so we log them.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.640
Everything after them is.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.177
AI paper trading exists.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:20.777
What's new: you coach it;
each version is signed on QIE.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.440
This one's an example.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.867
Other AI agents can check it too.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:29.630
Our read-only MCP server re-checks
a trade straight from QIE:

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.750
seven of seven prices match.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.120
We count users by who signed,
not what our servers send.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.740
Seasons are built to bring people back.
Next ninety days: our first hundred users.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.390
Built by Divesh, Gokul and Dijo,
for QIE Hackathon three.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.097
Raise an AI trader in one sentence,

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.800
coach it every season,
and let QIE keep score.
